 - 2026-06-18: PHASE C (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md; the DETECTOR compounds; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- does the verifier-as-DETECTOR SELF-IMPROVE / COMPOUND as labeled traces accumulate? The .402-.404 self-learning vehicle was the action-cost heuristic (exp4364 25->16) -- now SETTLED (exp4370 null). The LIVE vehicle is the detector (exp4375 AUROC 0.918; exp4381 makes it actionable). Apply the SAME compounding-curve discipline (the exp4364 pattern) to the detector: the detector's operating threshold + the BiPRM fusion weights are LEARNED and updated ONLINE as labeled (output, is_correct, step-label) traces accumulate; measure held-out detection localization-F1 / AUROC / selective-risk vs the accumulated-corpus SIZE (a monotone-improving learning curve), reproduction-gated, with a POSITIVE CONTROL (a from-scratch detector trained on the full corpus as the ceiling) and a NO-LEARNING baseline (the fixed-threshold detector). Emit detector_compounds BARE bool := (held-out localization-F1 / AUROC rises with corpus size BEYOND the no-learning baseline, CI95-excl-0, AND the positive control confirms the curve is not flat-because-saturated). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the detector vehicle COMPOUNDS (it gets better with data, like the action-cost heuristic did before it settled); a CLEAN null (the detector is already saturated on FoVer -> no learning headroom, confirmed by the positive control) is decision-grade and points to cross-domain (exp4386) for fresh headroom. Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: detector_compounds_heldout_localization_f1; results/experiment_4385_detector_self_learning_compounds.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE D (ORACLE-DISTINCT cross-domain DETECTION; complementary; cheap; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- does the verifier-as-DETECTOR GENERALIZE beyond FoVer? exp4375/exp4381 measured detection on FoVer ONLY (AUROC 0.918). The verifier is DOMAIN-BOUND (north-star §0 step 2 'verifier domain expansion'; memory verifier-domain-bound-math-only: math strong, facts/code weak); the .404 SOTA-ingestion's own failure-mode note: 'Math PRM gains can FAIL on FoVer or ARC traces'. Score the detector against a NON-FoVer cached corpus (the GAP-4 ARC pool results/arc3_trm_verifier_rerank.json; and/or the cached code HumanEval/MBPP / GSM8K candidate pools from the headroom census per the detector spec). Report detection AUROC + the SELECTION-headroom PER domain -- the headline is the DIVERGENCE (detect where you cannot select). Emit detector_generalizes_cross_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=1 NON-FoVer domain). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the detection capability is a GENERAL Carnot property (not FoVer-specific) -- the verifier-domain-expansion step; a domain where detection ~= chance is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (ops/verifier_gaps.md) -- that IS the product backlog. This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC where selection headroom is ~0), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: detector_generalizes_cross_domain_non_fover; results/experiment_4386_cross_domain_detection_generalization.json
